RSI4_PRIM,name=PREFER-MODE-VAL@ARBITRATE
RSI4_PRIMPROG,actions=GROUP-BY(val)>COUNT>EXTREMAL(count,GT)>SELECT-MATCH,place=ARBITRATE,stat=MODEVAL,use=PMAX
RSI4_PRIMTEXT,at M-ARBITRATE, when several facts share a key, group candidates by value (val), count each group, and prefer a fact whose value has the greatest count; ties fall back to baseline arbitration; action sequence GROUP-BY(val)>COUNT>EXTREMAL(count,GT)>SELECT-MATCH
RSI4_WRONG,place=ARBITRATE,stat=MODEVAL,use=PMIN
RSI4_WRONGREASON,selects the value with the smallest count (anti-mode); tempting rationale: the rare teaching is the deliberate correction and the repeated value is stale echo; measured D1 delta 0: cannot beat the first-wins baseline
